/* The knowledge cards and the screen words (handbook Part 159): DATA ONLY, read by claudian-cards.js.
   Written for the model, in English, and never shown to a person; the language audit does not read this file (tools/language-audit/surfaces.mjs).

   EACH CARD was drafted by one reader of the code and the handbook and then put to a second reader whose job was to refute it: 42 of 70 first
   drafts were corrected and none was kept as first written without a proof (test/claudian-cards.test.mjs holds what can be held by a test: the shape,
   the length, the screens each card is bound to, no person or company figure, no developer's word, and the few numbers the system itself fixes).
   WHEN A RULE CHANGES, the card that states it changes in the same commit (CHAT.md section 7).

   { id, tabs, where, leader, keys, text }
     tabs    the portal screens the card is about: a person is sent it only if they hold one of them ([] = anybody; only for what every officer is told).
     where   'both' | 'web' (the portal only) | 'phone' (HOPE Calls only).
     leader  true = only a leader's phone is sent it.
     keys    what a person types when they ask: Swahili and English words (three letters or fewer = a whole word; longer = a stem).
            KEYS WERE WIDENED on 25 Nov (handbook Part 159, addendum 1): six readers that saw only the cards wrote twelve questions for each (864) and proposed the words
            those questions imply; a word was kept only if it touched few questions about OTHER areas and none that is not about HOPE, and no key sits in more than six cards.
            A key that only one card has is enough to bring that card by itself, so a new key is a trigger: test/claudian-cards-retrieval.test.mjs holds the measured floors.
     text    how it works TODAY, English, at most 380 characters. */
